UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Ten of Pentacles represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Legacy''—the ultimate, multi-generational phase where the sovereign consciousness, having established individual autonomy (the Nine), integrates its achievements into an enduring, collective infrastructure that transcends the lifespan of the individual. Moving beyond the singular self-containment of the Nine, the Ten signifies the stage of ''The Sovereign Dynasty,'' where your personal resource cultivation successfully scales to support a broader ecosystem, family, or body of work that secures long-term systemic stability. Visually depicted as an elder surrounded by family, buildings, and loyal hounds within a secure courtyard, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Sovereign Intergenerational Wealth''—the realization that true material mastery is measured by the structural permanence of what you leave behind. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Institutional Integration,'' where individual micro-habits and insights crystallize into permanent, baseline operating structures that automate your well-being. When the Ten of Pentacles appears, your system is registering an ''Established Foundation'' status; you are being invited to stop the short-term, survivalist thinking and instead manage your life from the perspective of an enduring legacy. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your long-term architecture. You are being tasked with the essential work of ''Intentional Continuance'': ensuring that the frameworks, networks, and knowledge bases you are building are sturdy enough to outlast immediate situational shifts and serve as an unshakeable bedrock for the future.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Ten of Pentacles appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Rupture,'' ''Institutional Decay,'' or the catastrophic realization that your apparent structural security is being hollowed out by rigid traditionalism, internal friction, or a total failure of your legacy frameworks—a state where the structure you built to protect you has mutated into a stagnant, bureaucratic burden. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''preserving the past'' with ''ensuring safety,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a total, non-recoverable failure of its core evolutionary protocols. You are essentially ''clinging to an obsolete architecture,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''maintain a legacy facade'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually adapt to current-day realities. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''venerable patriarch or matriarch,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of alienation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency resentment, the experience of ''empty, hollow traditions,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your structural foundations are cracking under their own weight. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of structural stagnation''; you are obsessively trying to force old configurations to work, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final liberation of your energy is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to dismantle the legacy, you would be forced to acknowledge that your identity was anchored in old structures rather than living truth. The reversed Ten of Pentacles exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of ''structural dissolution,'' and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the ''imperishable monument'' and face the raw reality of your present-day, unanchored self, you would be forced to rebuild your security from scratch. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these rigid, legacy-bound, change-averse scripts, perform a brutal audit of your foundations, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize structural evolution over institutional comfort. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 52;
